**Definition 7.1 (binary actual-owner cycles).** Fix $d\ge3$ and a
cyclic length $n\ge4$. Let $s_i\in\{\alpha,\beta\}$ be owned at
the actual port $(i,L)$. Prescribe root factor $(0,0)$ and, at all
remaining targets in $W_d$,

$$
z_{i,Lr}=\Gamma_r(s_i),\qquad
z_{i,Rr}=\Gamma_r(s_{i+1}),
\qquad i\pmod n.
\tag{OOA.25}
$$

These are attained full-factor tables: their values are those of the
actual trees $\langle s_i,s_{i+1}\rangle\in S_d$. At the owner,
extend the leaf-factor table to branch and absent by the alpha factor;
its reply is alpha, excluding both forbidden inputs. Extend nonowner
tables arbitrarily within the target range. This gives total native
decoders and the required actual owner guards.

On the whole $S_d$ use the probability

$$
\mu(\langle a,b\rangle)=
\begin{cases}2/6,&a=b,\\1/6,&a\ne b,\end{cases}
\qquad a,b\in\{\alpha,\beta\},\qquad
\mu(x)=0\text{ otherwise}.
\tag{OOA.26}
$$

This is one full joint weight per original block. Its two-by-two weight
minor has determinant $1/12\ne0$, so it is not a product of leaf weights.

